<title>POLAND: Mostostal-Z jumps on GM contract.</title>
<headline>Mostostal-Z jumps on GM contract.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish builder Mostostal Zabrze SA jumped seven percent to 18.4 zlotys after Monday's news that Germany's Adam Opel AG, a General Motors unit, confirmed it would award Mostostal a 90 million mark contract, traders said.</p>
<p>The contract is for the construction of the main buildings at an Opel plant in Gliwice, southern Poland.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal definitely had an effect on the price today but it's not a sure thing because a contract hasn't been signed yet,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
